<!-- ════════════════ 14 · TRACK A · A2 INTRO ════════════════ -->
  <section data-label="A2: extend" class="slide light cat-themed" style="--c: #f472b6;">
    <div class="glow soft"></div>
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="cat-head">
        <span class="cat-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.12 2.12 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"/></svg>
        </span>
        <div class="cat-text">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">14</span>Track A &middot; extend</p>
          <h2 class="h2">Configure the agent once, <span class="accent">reuse it</span>.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="frame-body">
        <p style="font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 70ch; margin: 36px 0 32px;">Scoping gets the agent started well. Extending it lets every future session build on that foundation without repeating yourself.</p>
        <ul class="checklist" style="font-size: 22px; gap: 14px;">
          <li>Instructions: capture conventions once in a file the agent always reads.</li>
          <li>Commands and skills: package recurring workflows so you or the agent can invoke them.</li>
          <li>Subagents: give a scoped task its own context and tools.</li>
          <li>Hooks: automate guardrails on events (format, test, block).</li>
          <li>MCP: connect the agent to external tools and data.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% set slideNumber = "14" %}
    {% set slideTotal = "50" %}
    {% include "../../shared/chrome.njk" %}
  </section>
